# Database

- Every schema change requires a migration. Do not edit live schema by hand.
- Never alter production-critical tables without backward-compatibility analysis (reads and writes during deploy).
- Prefer additive migrations first (new columns/tables/indexes). Destructive changes (drop, rename, tighten constraints) come later and must be explicitly planned.
- Document indexes, foreign keys, unique constraints, and tenant boundaries in the migration or schema notes. Tenant-scoped tables: RLS + FORCE RLS.
- Sensitive tables need an audit strategy and retention notes (LGPD / privilégio jurídico — sem PII desnecessária em logs).
- Do not rewrite existing data implicitly. Any data backfill needs a rollback consideration.
- Seeds and fixtures must be deterministic (stable IDs, no `now()`-only uniqueness, no unordered random data).

```text
❌ Drop/rename column in the same deploy that still runs old code
✅ Add column → deploy readers/writers → backfill → remove old column in a later migration
```
